Note: `-` is both a built-in operator and a prefix for numbers — since `_is_number` is checked first, `-1` becomes a number and `-` alone becomes an operator. Good.

Definition check: name must not be a number → ValueError("illegal operation").

Edge case: `": 1 2 ;"` — tokens are `:`, `1`, `2`, `;`. Name `1` is a number → raise.

